<ns0:exercise xmlns:ns0="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:ns1="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="fs-id1167829749356" class="material-set-2">
<ns0:problem id="fs-id1167829749358">
<ns0:para id="fs-id1167829749361">The daily cost to the manufacturing company is modeled by the function <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>C</ns1:mi><ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>(</ns1:mo><ns1:mi>x</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>)</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>=</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>7.25</ns1:mn><ns1:mi>x</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>+</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>2500</ns1:mn></ns1:mrow></ns1:math> where <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>C</ns1:mi><ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>(</ns1:mo><ns1:mi>x</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>)</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow></ns1:mrow></ns1:math> is the total daily cost and <ns0:emphasis effect="italics">x</ns0:emphasis> is the number of items manufactured.</ns0:para>
<ns0:para id="fs-id1167829879667"><ns0:span class="token">ⓐ</ns0:span> Determine the independent and dependent variable.</ns0:para>
<ns0:para id="fs-id1167833272975"><ns0:span class="token">ⓑ</ns0:span> Find <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>C</ns1:mi><ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>(</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>0</ns1:mn><ns1:mo>)</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>.</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow></ns1:math> Explain what this result means.</ns0:para>
<ns0:para id="fs-id1167836494341"><ns0:span class="token">ⓒ</ns0:span> Find <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>C</ns1:mi><ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>(</ns1:mo><ns1:mrow><ns1:mn>1000</ns1:mn></ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>)</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>.</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow></ns1:math> Explain what this result means.</ns0:para>
</ns0:problem>
</ns0:exercise>
